        "created_at": "2012-07-11T20:17:12.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Well… That might be motivation for other areas to post their own events. <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=9\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\">  And maybe to <span class=\"bbcode-i\">create</span> their own events. <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=9\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\"></p>\n<p>Here’s hoping, anyway! 8)</p>\n<p>You’ll notice that all the Indy event threads were started by you and arenson9, though. (I’m not counting the GenCon/PAX Prime thread, only because it’s a large con and those are going to be different conversations.) If someone in another city posts about (or even getting directly involved with) their local cons, or posts about getting together at a local game shop, they’ll probably have growth similar to Indy’s.</p>\n<p>Rabit</p>",
